Familiarization of students with the basic principles of the concepts, techniques, and theory for the analysis of aerodynamic forces;
Development of various relevant skills and competences through the application of aerodynamics to the design of engineering components and systems;
Introduction to computational aerodynamics and panel methods codes for analysis of forces for general aircraft

This course will cover the fundamentals of geochemistry and geochemical thermodynamics, and demonstrate with the aid of examples their usefulness in magmatic and metamorphic petrology. The content is the following:
•	Fundamentals of thermodynamics and their application in the Earth Sciences;
•	Phase diagrams for igneous and metamorphic petrology;
Trace element and isotope geochemistry for igneous and metamorphic petrology.
